  "historical_output_text": " One day, while attending a writing seminar, I arrived late and my instructor, a well-known writer, began the session without me. Initially, I felt a mix of annoyance and embarrassment. I had been so focused on finding the perfect outfit for the day, I had overlooked the clock. The instructor greeted me with a warm smile and said, \"Sometimes, we all arrive late.\" He then proceeded to share a short anecdote about a time he was late and how it led to an unexpected and enriching meeting. This minor mistake reminded me of the importance of being present and open to the unexpected, not just in writing but in life. It's a lesson I carry with me, allowing me to be more adaptable and open to the journey rather than fixated on the destination. I left the seminar that day with a renewed perspective and a grateful heart",
